\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A representative inside the coefficient families}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{\ref{fdip-00AY} fixes the shapes #{t_N>1} that obey
#{T_q(t_{qN})=t_N} for every integer #{q\ge 2} and whose
difference #{t_N-1} is asymptotic to #{c/(2N^2)} with
#{c>0}. The shape is #{\cosh(m/N)} with #{c=m^2}. Along
that shape the neighbor scale is
#{\kappa\frac{m}{\sinh(m/N)}}, and the positive factor
#{\kappa} is free. \ref{fdip-00BA} identifies each marginal
of an arc-precision law, on at least two points, with the
arc-precision law of the remaining points.
\ref{fdip-00EB} gives the lower bound #{(m/N)^4/24} on the
difference between the fixed nearest-neighbor symbol shape
and #{\cosh(m/N)}. The three statements below keep the fixed
[finite-range circle precision](fdip-00C8) and one
nearest-neighbor choice whose rescaled field is the
equal-spacing arc law at every #{N\ge 3}.}
